{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Trigger CI/CD Pipeline",
  "description": "Automatically trigger GitHub Actions CI/CD pipeline when test-activation-handler is modified",
  "version": "2",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileSaved",
    "filePattern": "src/lambda/test-activation-handler/lambda/test-activation-handler/index.js"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The test-activation-handler Lambda function has been modified. Please execute this targeted CI/CD workflow:\n\n**Step 1: File Change Detection**\n1. Confirm that `src/lambda/test-activation-handler/lambda/test-activation-handler/index.js` was modified\n2. Check git status for this specific file\n3. Display the change summary for the test-activation-handler\n\n**Step 2: Git Status Verification**\n4. Check if the modified file has uncommitted changes\n5. If uncommitted changes exist:\n   - Show the git diff for the test-activation-handler file\n   - Ask if I want to commit the changes\n   - If yes, commit with: `git add src/lambda/test-activation-handler/lambda/test-activation-handler/index.js && git commit -m \"Update test-activation-handler Lambda function\"`\n   - Push to GitHub: `git push`\n6. If already committed, proceed to deployment\n\n**Step 3: Environment Selection**\n7. Ask which environment to deploy the test-activation-handler to:\n   - dev (default)\n   - staging\n   - prod\n8. Confirm the deployment target\n\n**Step 4: Trigger Targeted Deployment**\n9. Use the CI/CD trigger script specifically for test-activation-handler:\n   - `node scripts/trigger-cicd.js [environment] --lambda=test-activation-handler`\n10. This will:\n    - Trigger GitHub Actions workflow 'lambda-cicd.yml'\n    - Focus deployment on test-activation-handler only\n    - Skip unchanged Lambda functions for faster deployment\n11. Provide the GitHub Actions URL to monitor progress\n\n**Step 5: Deployment Monitoring**\n12. Monitor the test-activation-handler deployment:\n    - Use: `gh run watch` for real-time monitoring\n    - Show GitHub Actions workflow URL\n13. The pipeline will:\n    - Build and test the test-activation-handler code\n    - Package the Lambda function\n    - Deploy to AWS Lambda (test-activation-handler only)\n    - Update function configuration if needed\n    - Run post-deployment health checks\n\n**Step 6: Verification**\n14. After deployment completes:\n    - Verify the Lambda function is updated in AWS Console\n    - Check CloudWatch Logs for the test-activation-handler\n    - Confirm the function version/last modified timestamp\n    - Test the function if test endpoints are available\n\n**Step 7: Deployment Summary**\n15. Provide completion summary:\n    - Environment: [selected environment]\n    - Lambda function: test-activation-handler\n    - Deployment status: Success/Failed\n    - GitHub Actions run URL\n    - AWS Lambda function ARN\n    - Deployment time\n    - Next steps for verification\n\n**Important Notes:**\n- This hook is specifically triggered by changes to test-activation-handler\n- Only the test-activation-handler Lambda will be deployed (faster deployment)\n- The function handles test activation flows for the FOD system\n- Monitor CloudWatch Logs after deployment for any runtime errors\n- The function integrates with MongoDB, HTTP Bridge, and simulator services\n\nPlease execute this targeted workflow and keep me informed of the test-activation-handler deployment progress."
  }
}
